  "id": "mental-rotation",
  "term": "mental rotation",
  "definition": "Mental rotation is a spatial thinking ability in which a person forms a mental image of an object and imagines how it would look after being turned to a different orientation. It is used to recognize the same object from a new viewpoint.",
